      "title": "UK to deploy fighter jets to protect Saudi Arabia from Houthi attacks",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/20/uk-raf-typhoon-fighters-saudi-arabia-houthi-attacks",
      "description": "<p>RAF Typhoon fighters to fly defensive missions over cities and infrastructure in extension of UK support for Riyadh</p><p>RAF Typhoon fighters are to be used in efforts to protect Saudi Arabia from attack by Yemen’s Houthis, flying defensive missions over the country’s cities and critical infrastructure as western allies increase their intervention in the escalating conflict.</p><p>The operation – the most significant military mission signed off by Andy Burnham as prime minister – will involve RAF pilots attempting to shoot down Houthi missiles and drones, which attacked Saudi airports and oil facilities.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/oct/20/uk-raf-typhoon-fighters-saudi-arabia-houthi-attacks\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-20T11:54:52"
    },
